<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">trail</ansi>

Read the Trail is a ranger's skill. Each time your company walks into a
room, its best tracker reads the ground beyond the exits and tells you
which enemy groups lie that way, before you blunder into them. Only
hostile groups leave a report: players, companions, and peaceful folk
don't.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What each level reads</ansi>

  Level 1  which way: "fresh tracks, east"
  Level 2  who: "a band of ruffians, east"
  Level 3  how many: "a band of ruffians (3), east"
  Level 4  also two rooms away: "wolves (2), beyond north, then east"

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">On the road</ansi>

When you set out on a journey whose road can be ambushed, a tracker in
your company warns you as you leave. If the ambush comes, the tracker
leads the company off the road and around it, with a 20% chance per
level (80% at level 4). Then the ambushers never appear; you only find
their tracks. Otherwise the ambush happens as it would have.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">track</ansi>
  Read the trail here now, once a round. It works even with the
  automatic reading switched off.

  <ansi fg="command">autoskill trail off</ansi>
  Stop the reading on every step (<ansi fg="command">help autoskill</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help scout</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help travel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>.
